---
// Speaks to owners already paying a monthly subscription to a site builder.
// Leans on ownership and limits rather than raw price: maintenance plans are
// also monthly, so "stop paying monthly" would not be an honest pitch.
---

<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pt-20">
	<div class="rounded-lg border border-ink/10 bg-primary/5 p-8 sm:p-10">
		<h2 class="max-w-2xl font-head text-2xl font-semibold text-ink sm:text-3xl">
			Tired of paying every month for a site you don't love?
		</h2>
		<p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/75">
			If you're on Squarespace, Wix, or GoDaddy and the bill keeps arriving while the site
			still doesn't quite feel like yours, let's talk. I'll take an honest look at what
			you're paying for and tell you whether moving off it is worth it for your business.
			Sometimes it isn't, and I'll say so.
		</p>
		<a
			href="/contact"
			class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-semibold text-accent hover:underline"
		>
			Let's take a look →
		</a>
	</div>
</section>
